| **`(MaxInt, true)`** | **`incompatible_protocol`, exit 6** |\n\nTwo doc comments in the same diff say this must not happen (`:359-360`, `:403-404`), and the justifying paragraph names a narrower class than it enforces (\"an all-numeric giant\" — these aren't). The `foreignMajor` peek arms on the same predicate and **skips the entire v2 member-vocabulary check** for that class.\n\nNothing is admitted — but the killer is that **nothing measures it**: I applied the candidate fix (`major = math.MaxInt; continue`), the classification returns to spec, F2 stays closed, and the whole provhost suite passes unchanged. The shipped behaviour was never chosen; it fell out of the `return`.\n\nThe round-2 evidence cites the parse-arm census as proof nothing moved. That census enumerates *rejection branches*, so inputs moving **between** existing branches are invisible to it — a branch census is not an effect census.\n\nNotes (non-blocking): the AC ratio is 14 driven + 1 stated bound, reported as 15/15; the attestation tripwire matches `CallExpr` only; battery scripts live in `/tmp` instead of `.temp/<TASK-ID>/`.\n\nFull evidence attached as `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_review-verdict-rev2.md`.","ttft_ms":3249,"type":"result","duration_ms":1230020,"uuid":"da3d98c1-defc-417c-bcf1-dd6b9576ed90","ttft_stream_ms":2705,"time_to_request_ms":24,"first_content_frame_ms":2706,"queued_turn_count":0}
